redaction.refusals.body:
A redaction is also refused, with nothing changed, when:

- the ledger was never enabled, or is disabled;
- the caller has a transaction open;
- the graph name is invalid or the separator is empty;
- a redaction of another target has not finished ([rule](#redaction.batches.competing)).

redaction.receipt.body:
A redaction returns a receipt that says:

- whether the run completed, and a digest of the target;
- the seqs of the redacted revisions;
- how many records became tombstones, and how many revisions, idempotency keys and statement entries were cleared or removed;
- the redaction revision, once the run completes;
- what stays out of reach.

structure.adjacency.bulk.body:
A bulk path that writes rows without index upkeep must leave no duplicate rows and must rebuild the indexes before it returns, whether it succeeds or fails. Three paths do this:

- `bulk_create_nodes` and `bulk_create_edges`, which drop the indexes for a large batch and rebuild them afterwards;
- `bulk_load_session`;
- the bulk loader, whose own contract is on the [install page](../concepts/install.g5.md#install.bulk_load).

install.schema.not_ready.body:
An engine on a namespace with no schema record, or without the current release's SQL objects, raises one error on first access and runs nothing else. It never falls back to legacy objects. The error says which case applies and names setup and its dry run as the way forward:

- set up by an earlier release and not yet upgraded;
- never set up for IVG;
- a setup that stopped before finishing.
